WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.660
Berlin, the 1770s.

2
00:00:02.710 --> 00:00:06.320
A group of Jewish thinkers begins
a movement called the Haskalah,

3
00:00:06.370 --> 00:00:08.150
the Jewish Enlightenment.

4
00:00:08.200 --> 00:00:11.710
Their idea: Jews should join
European learning and culture,

5
00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:14.190
and still remain Jews.

6
00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:17.760
Over the next century, it
spread from Berlin to the east.

7
00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:22.140
So when Jews became citizens, did
they have to stop being a people?

8
00:00:22.190 --> 00:00:24.460
In this mission, you'll meet the Maskilim,

9
00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:28.020
with their new schools,
journals and revived Hebrew.

10
00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:30.750
Then you'll trace the new
movements that grew from it,

11
00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:33.690
and weigh up whether it
made Judaism stronger.

12
00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:38.350
Your mission: find out whether becoming
citizens meant Jews had to stop being

13
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:39.160
a people.
